                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi Top
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int^{[n]\in\Delta} S_{n,\bullet} \,\times\, \Delta^n_{Top}
          %p which will not, in general, agree with the diagonal and the abstract realization considered above. It does agree, however, after we pass to a further geometric realization as a single topological space.
          #RealizationOfDiagonalIsRealizationOfRealization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
