                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #RealizationOfSingularComplexIsWHE.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              For every
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Top
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %munder
                        %mi Sing
                        %mo ̲
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {|\underline{Sing}(X)|} \to X
                    \\,.
          %p#StricklandSeymour
            The proof can be found in
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"} Neil Strickland
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/q/171662/381"} mathoverflow question
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Seymour"} Seymour, prop. 3.1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi Sing
                    %mo ̲
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underline{Sing}(X)
            is proper. In fact, the first degeneracy map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi Top
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to [\Delta^1_{Top}, X]
            is not in general a cofibration as explained in the linked question.)
          %p Ordinary geometric realization has the following two disadvantages:
          #RealizationDoesntPreserveMCofibrancyOrHEs.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                  has in each degree the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
                  of a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert X_\bullet \vert}
                  in general need not.
              %li
                %p
                  If a morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon  X_\bullet \to Y_\bullet
                  is degreewise a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert f \vert}
                  need not be a homotopy equivalence.
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Segal74"}> Segal74, appendix A
            )
          %p This is different for the fat geometric realization.
          #NicePropertiesOfFatRealization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                  is degreewise of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
                  (i.e. is degreewise
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/m-cofibrant+space"} m-cofibrant
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert X_\bullet \Vert}
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon  X_\bullet \to Y_\bullet
                  is degreewise a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert f \Vert}
                  is a homotopy equivalence.
          %p
            This appears as (
            %a{:href => "#Segal"}> Segal74, prop. A.1
            ).
          %h3#relation_between_fat_and_ordinary_geometric_realization Relation between fat and ordinary geometric realization
          %p
          #FatRealizationOfGoodSimplicialSpaces.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
            %p
              If the simplicial topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              is
              %a{:href => "#GoodAndProper"} good
              then the natural morphism from its
              %a{:href => "#FatGeometricRealization"} fat geometric realization
              to its
              %a{:href => "#GeometricRealization"} ordinary geometric realization
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\Vert X_\bullet \Vert} \stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow} {|X_\bullet|}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            A direct proof of this (not using that
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoodImpliesProper"} good implies proper
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Segal74"} Segal74, prop. A.1 (iv)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#tomDieck74"} tom Dieck 1974, Prop. 1
          %p
            A recent paper treating the special case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
            is the nerve of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+category"} topological category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
            is of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Wang17"} Wang 2017
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Wang18"} Wang 18
          %h3#CompatibilityWithLimits Compatibility with limits
          %p
            We discuss how geometric realization interacts with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            of simplicial topological spaces.
          %h4#ordinary_geometric_realization Ordinary geometric realization
          #RealizationPreservesPullbacks.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (geometric realization prerserves pullbacks)
              %br/
            %p
              In the category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mo ←
                    %msub
                      %mi Z
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \to Y_\bullet \leftarrow Z_\bullet
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\Delta^{op}}
              there are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphisms"} homeomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi Z
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ×
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Y
                            %mo •
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Z
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {|X_\bullet|} \,\times_{|Y_\bullet|}\, {|Z_\bullet|}
                    \\simeq
                    {|X_\bullet \,\times_{Y_\bullet}\, Z_\bullet|}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#May72"}> May 1972, Cor. 11.6
            ). See also the proof that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            (
            %a{:href => "geometric+realization#GeometricRealizationIsLeftExact"}> here
            ).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              It is essential in Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealizationPreservesPullbacks"}
              to work in a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              such as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactly+generated+topological+spaces"} compactly generated topological spaces
              (also “k-spaces”): in the category of
              %em all
              topological spaces the proposition would not be true. It works in these cases because product and/or quotient topologies in these categories are slightly different from in the category of all topological spaces.
          %p It follows that:
          %p
          #GeometricRealizationPreservesFiniteLimits.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Geometric realization of simplicial compactly-generated topological spaces preserves all
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "finite+limit#FiniteLimitsFromPullbacksAndTerminalObject"} this Prop.
              finite limits are preserved as soon as
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  is preserved, which here is evidently the case;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
                  are preserved, which is the case by Prop.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealizationPreservesPullbacks"}
            %p
          %h4#fat_geometric_realization Fat geometric realization
          %p
            The operation of
            %a{:href => "#FatGeometricRealization"} fat geometric realization
            does not preserve
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\Vert * \Vert}
            for the fat geometric realization of the point. Notice that due to the identification of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sTop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sTop
            with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            over the point (the simplicial topological space constant on the point),
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sTop
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi sTop
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sTop\simeq sTop/*
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top/{\Vert*\Vert}
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GeometricRealizationOfThePoint"} fat geometric realization of the point
          %p
          #FatRealizationPreservesConnectedFiniteLimits.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p The functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo *
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\Vert - \Vert} \colon  Top^{\Delta^{op}} \to Top/{\Vert*\Vert}
            %p
              preserves all
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
          %p
            This is claimed in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GepnerHenriques07"} Gepner-Henriques 07, Remark 2.23
          %h3#PreservationOfHomotopyLimits Preservation of homotopy limits
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
          %p
          #SufficientConditionsForRealizationToPreserveHomotopyPullback.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserved
                by geometric realization)
              %br/
              For a morphism of simplicial spaces
            #eq:AMorphismOfSimplicialTopologicalSpacesToBeHomotopyPulledBack.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f_\bullet \,\colon\, X_\bullet \xrightarrow{\;} Y_\bullet
                    \\,,
            %p
              the following are sufficient conditions for the geometric realization of any
              = succeed "-square" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\bullet
              to be a
              = succeed "-square" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
            %ol
              %li#BousfieldFriedlanderPiStarKanCondition
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#BousfieldFriedlander78"}> Bousfield &amp; Friedlander 1978, Thm. B.4
                  \:
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      on
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                      of
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(f)_\bullet
                      is a
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
                  %li
                    %p
                      the simplicial spaces
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mo •
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
                      and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mo •
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_\bullet
                      satisfy the
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%CF%80-Kan+condition"} π-Kan condition
              %li
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#Anderson78"}> Anderson 1978, p. 2
                  \:
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      on
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
                      of
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(f)_\bullet
                      is a
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
                  %li
                    %p
                      the component spaces
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mi n
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_n
                      (
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi ℕ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                      ) are each
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
                      or
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+space"} discrete
              %li#RezkConditionForPreservationOfHomotopyPullbacks
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#Rezk14"}> Rezk 2014, Prop. 5.4
                  \:
                %ul
                  %li
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
                    of the base is
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Y
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi const
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi π
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                              %mo •
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(Y)_\bullet \simeq const\big(\pi_0(Y_0)\big)_\bullet
                %p
                  This is also essentially
                  %a{:href => "#LurieHigherAlgebra"} Lurie HA, Lem. 5.5.6.17
                  (using that simplicial
                  = succeed "-colimits" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sifted+infinity-colimit"} sifted
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a{:href => "sifted+infinity-colimit#SimplicialInfinityColimitsAreSifted"} this Prop.
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-toposes"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                    \-toposes
                  other than
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi L
                            %mi W
                          %mi Top
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_W Top
              %li#KanLikeFibrationConditionForPreservationOfHomotopyPullbacks
                %p
                  %a{:href => "#MazelGee14"}> Mazel-Gee 2014, Cor. 6.7
                  ,
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a{:href => "#Lurie11"} Lurie 2011, Prop. 10
                %ul
                  %li
                    the morphism
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:AMorphismOfSimplicialTopologicalSpacesToBeHomotopyPulledBack"} (1)
                    is a
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+Kan+fibration"} homotopy Kan fibration
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+numbers"} positive numbers
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi ℕ
                            %mo +
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}_+
                    and all
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi k
                          %mo ≤
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \leq n
                    the induced map
                #eq:HomotopyTheoreticKanFibration.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Λ
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %munder
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mo ×
                              %mi h
                          %mrow
                            %mi Y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Λ
                              %mi k
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        X(\Delta^n)
                        \\xrightarrow{\;\;}
                        X(\Lambda^n_k)
                        \\underset
                        { Y(\Lambda^n_k) }
                        {\times^h}
                        Y(\Delta^n)
                %p
                  (into the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
                  of the space of space of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horns"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi n
                          %mo ,
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,k)
                    \-horns
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
