              %path{:d => "M -1.553792 3.068408 C -0.799388 1.447247 1.228546 0.0589994 2.385146 -0.000125815 C 1.229489 -0.0575349 -0.79938 -1.450195 -1.552981 -3.067584 ", :fill => "none", :stroke => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "stroke-linecap" => "round", "stroke-linejoin" => "round", "stroke-miterlimit" => "10", "stroke-opacity" => "1", "stroke-width" => "0.47818", :transform => "matrix(-0.64308, 0.76576, 0.76576, 0.64308, 92.93628, 36.2166)"}
              %g{"clip-path" => "url(#rDlaC27jhvuHOPUXlky_Y_RNj7U=-clip-0)"}
                %path{:d => "M -1.755719 -6.672062 L -16.58775 -24.457219 ", :fill => "none", :stroke => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "stroke-dasharray" => "3.34735 1.91277", "stroke-linecap" => "butt", "stroke-linejoin" => "miter", "stroke-miterlimit" => "10", "stroke-opacity" => "1", "stroke-width" => "2.79451", :transform => "matrix(1, 0, 0, -1, 87.119, 45.617)"}
              %g{"clip-path" => "url(#rDlaC27jhvuHOPUXlky_Y_RNj7U=-clip-1)"}
                %path{:d => "M -1.755719 -6.672062 L -16.58775 -24.457219 ", :fill => "none", :stroke => "rgb(100%, 100%, 100%)", "stroke-dasharray" => "3.34735 1.91277", "stroke-linecap" => "butt", "stroke-linejoin" => "miter", "stroke-miterlimit" => "10", "stroke-opacity" => "1", "stroke-width" => "1.83812", :transform => "matrix(1, 0, 0, -1, 87.119, 45.617)"}
              %path{:d => "M -1.552788 3.067493 C -0.79793 1.448709 1.228287 0.0559733 2.385209 -0.00162016 C 1.226328 -0.0575668 -0.799363 -1.446795 -1.551025 -3.070636 ", :fill => "none", :stroke => "rgb(0%, 0%, 0%)", "stroke-linecap" => "round", "stroke-linejoin" => "round", "stroke-miterlimit" => "10", "stroke-opacity" => "1", "stroke-width" => "0.47818", :transform => "matrix(-0.64043, 0.76794, 0.76794, 0.64043, 70.53271, 70.07559)"}
            %p
          %h3#RelationToHomotopyColimit Relation to the homotopy colimit
          %h4#for_proper_simplicial_spaces For proper simplicial spaces
          %p
            Recall that a simplicial topological space is proper if it is Reedy cofibrant relative to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Str%C3%B8m+model+structure"} Strøm model structure
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \colon  \Delta^{op} \to Top
            given by the simplicial space, with respect to the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} Quillen model structure on topological spaces
            in which the weak equivalences are the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
          #RealizPresWHE.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \to Y_\bullet
              is an objectwise weak homotopy equivalence between proper simplicial spaces, then the induced map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi Y
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X_\bullet|} \to {|Y_\bullet|}
              is a weak homotopy equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              The following proof is essentially from (
              %a{:href => "#May_Einf"}> May 1974, A.4
              ); see also (
              %a{:href => "#Dugger"}> Dugger, prop. 17.4, example 18.2
              ). It relies on two facts relating
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+cofibration"} Hurewicz cofibration
              = succeed "s:" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} Pushouts
                  along
                  = succeed "s" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+cofibration"} Hurewicz cofibration
                  = succeed "s," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} Colimits
                  of sequences of Hurewicz cofibrations preserve weak homotopy equivalences.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_n \colon \Delta_{\le n} \hookrightarrow \Delta
              denote the inclusion of the objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \le n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %msubsup
                        %mi i
                        %mi n
                        %mo *
                      %mi Δ
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Δ
                            %mrow
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi n
                      %msubsup
                        %mi i
                        %mi n
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X_\bullet|}_n = i_n^* \Delta \otimes_{\Delta_{\le n}} i_n^* X_\bullet
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_n X
              for the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/latching+object"} latching object
              (the subspace of degeneracies in
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mi n
                            %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi L
                                  %mi n
                                %mi X
                                %mo ×
                                %mo ∂
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %mo ∂
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi n
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mi n
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %msub
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo •
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ (L_n X \times \Delta^n) \sqcup_{L_n X \times \partial\Delta^n} (X_n \times \partial\Delta^n) &amp; \to &amp;  {|X_\bullet|}_{n-1}\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow\\
                    X_n \times \Delta^n &amp; \to &amp;  {|X_\bullet|}_n }
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is proper,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_n X \to X_n
              is a cofibration, and of course
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial\Delta^n \to \Delta^n
              is a cofibration. Thus, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
              for the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Str%C3%B8m+model+structure"} Strøm model structure
            %p
              Now
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X_\bullet|}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of the sequence of cofibrations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X_\bullet|}_0 \to {|X_\bullet|}_1 \to {|X_\bullet|}_2 \to \cdots
            %p
              and likewise for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|Y_\bullet|}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtration"} filtered
              by simplicial degree. Thus, by point (2) above, it suffices to show that each map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi Y
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X_\bullet|}_n \to {|Y_\bullet|}_n
              is a weak homotopy equivalence.
            %p
              Since
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X_\bullet|}_0 = X_0
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X_\bullet|}_n
              is a pushout of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|X_\bullet|}_{n-1}
              along a cofibration. Thus, by point (1) above, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_n \times \Delta^n \to Y_n \times \Delta^n
              is certainly a weak homotopy equivalence, it will suffice for an induction step to prove that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi n
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi n
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mi n
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ×
                        %mo ∂
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
