                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} hocolim
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hocolim
              doesn’t depend on the choice of an objectwise-cofibrant replacement of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              to be, instead of the composite with a functorial cofibrant replacement in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Top
                        %mi Quillen
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top^{\Delta^{op}}
              with respect to the Quillen model structure on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Top
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q X_\bullet
              is Quillen-Reedy cofibrant, hence also proper, and so the Bousfield-Kan map is a homotopy equivalence. On the other hand,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q X_\bullet \to X_\bullet
              is a levelwise weak homotopy equivalence, while
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q X_\bullet
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
              are proper, so by Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RealizPresWHE"}
              its realization is a weak homotopy equivalence.
          %p By naturality, the above composite is also equal to the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
