          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              This global notion of topological Kan fibration is considered in (
              %a{:href => "#BrownSzczarba"}> Brown &amp; Szczarba, def. 2.1, def. 6.1
              ). In fact there a stronger condition is imposed: a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              automatically has the lifting property not only against all full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
              inclusions but also against sub-horns; and in (
              %a{:href => "#BrownSzczarba"}> Brown &amp; Szczarba
              ) all these fillers are required to be given by global sections. This ensures that with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              globally Kan also the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sTop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Y,X] \in sTop
              is globally Kan, for any simplicial topological space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is globally Kan in the sense of (
              %a{:href => "#BrownSzczarba"}> Brown &amp; Szczarba, def. 6.1
              ), then it is so also in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#GloballyKanSimplicialTopologicalSpace"} above sense
          %p
            Recall from the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} universal principal ∞-bundle
            that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+topological+group"} simplicial topological group
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+simplicial+principal+bundle"} universal simplicial principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
